add(R, passage(P, ARTSAG108, `위 글의 빈칸 (A)에 들어갈 말로 알맞은 것은?`), '1', ['Art imitates nature', 'Nature is our mother', 'Youth is the gift of nature', 'Colors are the smiles of nature', "To the artist, there's never anything ugly."]);
add(R, passage(P, ARTSAG108, `위 글의 밑줄 친 (B)의 우리말을 아래와 같이 영작할 때, 두 번째 빈칸에 오는 말로 알맞은 것은?\n\n→ ________ ________ ________ ________ its ________`), '4', ['to', 'strong', 'protect', 'enough', 'contents']);
add(R, passage(P, `In the first two examples, we can easily see what inspired the architect. But in the next example from Australia, this is not so (A)________. Jørn Utzon, the architect of the Sydney Opera House, took a shape from nature and added his imagination. ⓐ<u>Can you guess what inspired him?</u> ⓑ<u>Many people think that it is the waves in the ocean or a sailing boat.</u> ⓒ<u>But interestingly, the inspiration actually came from a sailing boat.</u> ⓓ<u>Look at the roof closely.</u> ⓔ<u>Can you see the peels of an orange?</u> When orange lights are shone on the building, you can see the peels more clearly.`, `위 글을 읽고 다음 질문에 답하시오.\n\nWhat did Jørn Utzon do after taking a shape from nature to design the Sydney Opera House? Fill in the blank.\n\n→ He ________ ________ ________.`), 'added his imagination', null);
add(R, `다음 글의 Boram Middle School에 대한 설명으로 가장 적절한 것은?\n\nI go to Boram Middle School in Suwon. My school has a 4-story building. It also has a large playground, a gym and a small garden. The garden is on top of the school building. We grow some vegetables there so that we can have fresh food. My favorite place is the bench under the big tree. I love sitting there and talking with my friends. I like my school very much.`, '5', ['우리 학교에는 네 가지 이야기가 있다.', '학교 가장 위층에는 커다란 체육관이 있다.', '내가 좋아하는 장소는 큰 나무로 만든 벤치이다.', '나는 교실에 앉아 친구들과 이야기 나누는 것을 좋아한다.', '학교에는 넓은 운동장과 체육관, 작은 정원이 있다.']);

