add(R, `다음 문장의 빈칸에 Sam과 Emily 각각의 저축 목적을 <조건>에 알맞게 쓰시오.\n\n<조건>\n(1)번은 order, (2)번은 so that을 반드시 포함할 것\n\n(1) Sam saved money ______________________. (Sam의 저축 목적: 아픈 사람들을 도와주기 위해)\n(2) Emily saved money ______________________. (Emily의 저축 목적: 새로운 핸드폰을 구매하기 위해)`, 'in order to help sick people / so that she could buy a new phone', null, { subParts: sp(['in order to help sick people', 'so that she could buy a new phone']) });
add(R, `다음 대화의 밑줄 친 문장과 의미가 다른 것은?\n\nA: Hi, Lisa. <u>Thank you for inviting me to your birthday party</u>.\nB: My pleasure. I'm glad you could come.`, '3', ['I appreciate your invitation.', "I'm grateful to you for the invitation.", "I don't understand why you invite me.", "I'm very thankful to you for inviting me.", "I can't tell you how much your invitation means to me."]);
add(R, `다음 두 대화의 빈칸에 공통으로 들어갈 말로 알맞은 것은?\n\nA: How was the movie?\nB: It was great. Thank you for recommending the movie.\nA: You're welcome. ______________________\n\nA: Thank you for inviting me to your birthday party.\nB: ______________________ I'm happy you could come.\nA: These flowers are for you. Happy birthday!\nB: They are beautiful. Thank you.`, '1', ['My pleasure.', "I'll try my best.", 'I hope you do well.', "I'm sorry. I didn't know that.", "You need to listen carefully to others' opinions."]);
add(R, `다음 글의 밑줄 친 ⓐ~ⓔ 중, 흐름상 어색한 것은?\n\nHello, students! ⓐ<u>Thank you for visiting our art museum</u>. This museum opened in 1995. ⓑ<u>Since then, it has exhibited many famous artworks</u>. ⓒ<u>Today, you will see some famous artworks from the art books</u>. Before we begin the tour, let me remind you of a basic rule. ⓓ<u>You can take pictures of the artworks, but you're not allowed to touch them</u>. ⓔ<u>You can feel artworks by breaking them</u>. Now let's start the tour.`, '5', CIRCLE);
